                <pb facs="1283" n="1087" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1087"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1094<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied
                        Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-17">July 17, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi>–51. To Kindleberger and Wolf, White
                    House, Washington for [Acting] Secretary of State from Pauley.</p>
                <p>Understand that Reinstein has been preparing materials on possible Italian
                    reparations and restitutions. Urgently require outstanding features of this
                    report. Cable summary to me at Tripartite Conference Headquarters <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Masterwork</hi> Berlin with particular emphasis upon
                    what might be available for reparations and possible value of same. Send also
                    estimates made by State and FEA as to value of imports required by Italy in
                    order to maintain her economy over the coming year. (Repeat message for Sproul,
                    c/o American Delegation, Allied Commission on Reparations, American Embassy,
                    Moscow, for his information numbering the repeat message as follows <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Confrep</hi> 3.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
